! gitignore-style ignores:
! Keep all aerochem_vmr_* rows (incl. num_a2/c2):
!   this is the raw capture of the VMR array after the gasaerexch+rename block.
! EXCLUDE num_a2, num_c2 constituent rows:
!   the MMR -> VMR -> MMR round-trip is inherently diff-generating:
!   CAM converts the applied sum fl((vmr+d*dt)*a)
!   SIMA VMR unpack applies the converted tendency in the MMR space
!        fl(vmr*a)+fl(dt*fl(d*a))
!   Most of these differences are absorbed by the 2e-15 min_difference,
!   except for the aitken numbers, since the "rename" (mode merging) scheme
!   physically merges aitken (2) -> accum (1) mode leading to very low VMRs
!   strongly susceptible to noise.
! Naturally included: del_h2so4_aeruptk, all other constituents
!
! If running with debug, that is all you need. The snapshot is made with debug.
!
! --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!       Technical notes for the brave reader who is considering changing
!                         this test to a non-_D test:
!
! If disabling debug, the -O2 flag will optimize the paths differently enough to
! cause a O(1e-14) drift in aerochem_vmr_num_a4 (even in VMR space).
!
! A dropsonde verification with a custom-built "-g -O2" binary has verified that
! the outputs for modal_aero_gasaerexch_run drift by O(1e-14) for dqdt/qsrflx_gaexch
! even when given identical inputs. They disappear at O0.
!
! The verification run was made by Haipeng who also stubbornly hand-verified
! the assembly to confirm that it is indeed a -O2 problem.
!
! Specifically, -O2 inlines gas_aer_uptkrates and vectorizes the nghq=2
! Gauss-Hermite quadrature. The dp = exp(lndp) is compiled into libmvec SIMD
! covering both quadrature points. libmvec does not guarantee bit-identical to
! the scalar version. This shifts the H2SO4/SOAG uptake rates...
! ...which in turn perturbs the condensation amounts on aerosol
!    (H2SO4 -> so4_a1/2/3, SOAG -> soa_a1/2)
!    and the primary-carbon aging transfers (bc/pom/num_a4 -> a1)
! Primary-carbon aging drains most of the local num_a4 primary carbon mode number,
! leaving it, again, susceptible to a large relative difference. There are 45 cells
! in this snapshot in which this happens, and their end value is O(1e-15).
!
! tl;dr: If you disable debug, you have to add '*num_a4' to the exclude list below:
ncdata_check_exclude = '!aerochem_vmr_*', '*num_a2', '*num_c2'
ncdata_check_err = .true.
min_difference = 2e-15

